igh outer rim!\n   - **Key Landmarks from `#32` (for Set-Pieces & `--preview` Shots)**:\n     - `canyon_grid`: `s = 0..596 m` (`f = 1..224`), Chicane Apex `idx=199` (`s=398 m`, `f=125`).\n     - `eau_rouge_climb`: `s = 596..1228 m` (`f = 224..422`), Bottom Spark Compression `idx=392` (`s=784 m`, `f=282`, `318.5 km/h`), Steepest Climb `idx=437` (`+13.51°` pitch, `f=309`), **`+42.0 m` Blind Crest `idx=599` (`s=1198 m`, `f=414`)** -> make sure `_crest_idx = 599` (where `V6_HorizonMoonPortal` is aimed along `FRAMES[599][\"fwd\"]` so `@anim`'s `300 mm` blind-crest silhouette shot at `f=414` frames the giant moon directly behind the cresting car!).\n     - `sky_bridge`: `s = 1228..1860 m` (`f = 422..604`, `bridge=True`, `316` pts / `632 m`, `Z = 42.0..42.4 m`).\n     - `banked_bowl_plunge`: `s = 1860..2604 m` (`f = 604..898`), **`188°` Carousel `+17.4°` Banked Apex `idx=974` (`s=1948 m`, `f=635`)**, Corkscrew `-13.94°` Plunge `idx=1189` (`s=2378 m`, `f=830`).\n     - `strobe_tunnel_harbor`: `s = 2604..3720 m` (`f = 898..1281`), **Enclosed Cyber-Strobe Tunnel `idx=1321..1581` (`s=2642..3162 m`, `520 m`, `f=908..1041`, top speed `341.2 km/h`)**, Harbor Hairpin Heavy-Brake Slam `idx=1631` (`s=3262 m`, `f=1067`) -> Hairpin Apex `idx=1687` (`s=3374 m`, `f=1134`, `81.1 km/h`).\n   - **Blender 5.3.0 EEVEE Shader & Driver Rules Discovered**:\n     - **Input-Socket Drivers Only**: EEVEE caches `ShaderNodeValue.outputs[0].default_value` as a compile-time constant! All `scene[\"sv_dimension\"]` drivers MUST be placed on **INPUT** sockets (e.g. `grp.inputs[\"SV Dimension\"]`, `ShaderNodeMath.inputs[0]`), and `scene['[\"sv_dimension\"]']` must be keyframed when testing across frames. (`v6_sv_env.py` already uses input-socket drivers!).\n     - **Wet Road Without Sun Wedge**: `sun.data.specular_factor = 0.0` + `fill.data.specular_factor = 0.0` with `scene.eevee.use_raytracing = True` eliminates any white solar specular wedge on the road while preserving crisp raytraced reflections of emissive skyscrapers, stay-cables, tunnel laser ribs, and car lights in `MAT_V6_WetAsphalt` (`Roughness = 0.065..0.255`).\n     - **Car Rig & Material Conventions (`v4_stage_rig.blend`)**:\n       - Car local forward is `+Y`, right is `+X`, up is `+Z`, so 3D car rotation matrix columns in world space are `(R, T, U)` (`Matrix(((R.x, T.x, U.x), (R.y, T.y, U.y), (R.z, T.z, U.z)))`).\n       - `GEO_F1_FrontWing_Endplate_L/R` has non-uniform scale `(0.018, 0.62, 0.36)` (skip `Solidify` when `min(scale) < 0.15`), and `Mirror_X` meshes require `Solidify.use_rim = False` to avoid centerline black walls.\n       - Keep `Mat_Brake_HeatGlow` at its 2-node baseline (`Emission` + `Output`), `Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic` with radial `Emission Color` ramp & undriven `Emission Strength = 0.0`, `Mat_Caliper_Anodized` undriven, and single-user `Mat_FIA_RainLight` on `GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight` so `@anim`'s `v6_sv_comp.py` hooks in cleanly.\n     - **Chinese Locale Node Names**: Never look up nodes by English display name (`nt.nodes['Value']` throws `KeyError` in Chinese locale); always keep Python variable references or filter by `n.type`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Media Attachment 400 Error (`#7`)**: Calling `read_file` on any binary/image/media file (`.jpg`, `.png`, `.mp4`, `.wav`, `.m4a`, `.blend`) bricks the conversation (`env` died to this). **Fix**: Strictly inspect images via system `python` (`PIL`/`numpy`) and `.blend` files via headless Blender scripts.\n   - **PowerShell `--python-expr` Quote Escaping**: Escaped quotes inside inline PowerShell `--python-expr` caused `SyntaxError`. **Fix**: Write helper/inspection scripts to `C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b13776a0-7d9f-4f63-9e67-c8ecc5f11412\\scratch\\*.py` and invoke with `-P`.\n   - **Bundled Blender Python Lacks `PIL`**: Importing `PIL` inside Blender's Python failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`. **Fix**: Run `PIL`/`numpy` image verification scripts using system `python`, not Blender's embedded Python.\n  