FRAMES` construction, lines 40–76 of `pipeline/v6_sv_env.py`), replace the heuristic `_BANK_SAME_SIGN` frame builder with `@track`'s exact formula from `#32`:\n        ```python\n        h = radians(pt[\"heading_deg\"])\n        p = radians(pt.get(\"pitch_deg\", 0.0))\n        bk = radians(pt.get(\"bank_deg\", 0.0))\n        fwd = Vector((cos(p) * cos(h), cos(p) * sin(h), sin(p))).normalized()\n        right0 = Vector((sin(h), -cos(h), 0.0)).normalized()\n        up0 = Vector((-sin(p) * cos(h), -sin(p) * sin(h), cos(p))).normalized()\n        right = (cos(bk) * right0 - sin(bk) * up0).normalized()\n        up = (sin(bk) * right0 + cos(bk) * up0).normalized()\n        ```\n        (Store `bk` in `fr[\"bk\"]` / `fr[\"b_eff\"]`).\n      - In Section 5 (`_crest_idx`, around line 347), pin `_crest_idx` to the `eau_rouge_climb` crest (`idx = 599` or max `pos.z` inside `zone == \"eau_rouge_climb\"` before `sky_bridge`, and place `V6_HorizonMoonPortal` along `FRAMES[_crest_idx][\"fwd\"]` horizontal projection at an elevation angle of `~6°–8°` above the `+42 m` crest so a `135–300 mm` camera looking uphill from `idx ~ 575..595` frames the giant glowing moon/portal right behind the cresting car!).\n      - In Section 7 (`V6_BankedBowl_NeonWall`, around line 551), set `out_sgn = 1.0 if fb0[\"right\"].z >= 0.0 else -1.0` (whenever `abs(math.degrees(fb0[\"b_eff\"])) > 6.5`), so the `4.2 m` curved neon wall sits on the **raised outer rim** of the `+17.4°` right-hand bowl (`sgn = -1.0`, since `bk > 0` makes `(-right).z > 0`)!\n      - Also double-check skyscraper/pier clearance in `build_five_setpieces()`: verify `min_xy_dist_to_track` checks distance to ALL `FRAMES[k][\"pos\"]` so zero buildings or piers ever intrude into any track corridor, bridge, or tunnel!\n      - In Section 9 (`--preview`), set the 5 preview indices to `@track`'s exact `#32` landmarks (`i_canyon = 120`, `i_crest = 592` looking uphill through `599` at the Horizon Moon!, `i_bridge = 750`, `i_bowl = 974`, `i_t